<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/03c93409604c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[5064] Microsoft said last year that it wouldn’t sell its facial recognition software to police departments until the federal government regulates such systems." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5064" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/045c1638cc47> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[5064] Amazon announced a one-year moratorium on allowing police forces to use its facial recognition technology." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5064" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0aaa1469e780> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1458] Last year, NBC News reported the company had been using its customers’ photos to develop facial recognition technology that it turned around and offered for sale by way of the Ever API to business clients, including law enforcement and the military." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1458" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0dd3a246594c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1458] Last year, NBC News reported the company had been using its customers’ photos to develop facial recognition technology..." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1458" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/11d67eaddb4f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[5064] Facebook agreed to pay $550 million last year to settle a class-action lawsuit alleging the company violated an Illinois privacy law with its facial recognition activities." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5064" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/13e4a55ddd4b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[5064] Amazon announced a one-year moratorium on allowing police forces to use its facial recognition technology." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5064" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/157ff5924944> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[5064] The powers that be at UCLA thought it was a good idea at the time — using state-of-the-art technology to scan students’ faces for gaining access to campus buildings." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5064" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/192f318d0cb4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The report found that the Ever app was using customer’s private photos to train its facial recognition algorithm, which it then sold to clients." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8646" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1e0ef9132974> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[8646] Photo services often use facial recognition to classify photos — Google, Facebook, and Apple have all been criticized in the past for their systems over privacy concerns..." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8646" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1e9401175f64> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[5064] The powers that be at UCLA thought it was a good idea at the time — using state-of-the-art technology to scan students’ faces for gaining access to campus buildings." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5064" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1ea1fc93e8d5> a airo:Evidence ;
